## mcp-network Development Conventions

### Inventory & secrets

- Fleet metadata lives in `inventory/sites/*.json` and is validated against
  `inventory/schema/site.schema.json`. **Never** put credentials in those
  files — each site declares the *names* of the env vars that hold its
  SSH user / password via `credentials_env`.
- Adding a site is inventory + env only; it must not require a code change.
- When referencing a site in code or docstrings, prefer the site key
  (`ori`) over ad-hoc labels.

### Site resolution

- Tools take an optional `site: str | None = None`. Resolution precedence:
  explicit `site` arg > switch-name lookup across all sites > default site
  (`NETWORK_DEFAULT_SITE` env wins over inventory `default: true`).
- Raise a clear error if a switch is ambiguous across sites; do not silently
  pick one.

### Drivers

- One driver per switch OS under `mcp_network/drivers/`. Implement the
  `SwitchDriver` ABC from `drivers/base.py`. Dispatch is via
  `get_driver(site_cfg, switch)` keyed on `site_cfg.driver`.
- All network I/O is `async`. Open SSH per command; jump-host tunneling is
  handled in `drivers/cumulus._open`.
- Validate port names with `_validate_port` before building any shell
  command — defense-in-depth against injection.
- Raise `NetworkDriverError` (with `host=` and `hint=` when useful) on
  every failure path. Tools translate those to `RuntimeError` for the
  MCP response.

### Tools

- All tools must have descriptive docstrings (MCP uses them as tool
  descriptions).
- Use type hints on every parameter; prefer `Annotated[T, Field(description=...)]`
  so the parameter doc propagates to MCP clients.
- Return structured dicts, not formatted strings.
- **Strictly read-only.** Never expose tools that mutate switch state
  (no config changes, no reboots, no port toggles). Mark every tool with
  `annotations={"readOnlyHint": True}`.

### Errors

- Tool-level: raise `RuntimeError(str(e))` from caught `NetworkDriverError` or
  `KeyError`. This lets FastMCP serialize a clear error to the client.
- Never log raw credentials or anything derived from `SecretStr.get_secret_value()`.
